From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rzg2l-smarc-som: pin mmc aliases for deterministic
 mmcblk numbering

The kernel mmc core registers SDHI controllers in async-probe order.
On the RZ/V2L SMARC SoM both sdhi0 (mmc@11c00000, the boot-side SD/eMMC
slot) and sdhi1 (mmc@11c10000) are status="okay", so whichever finishes
probe first gets mmcblk0. The result is that a bare
"root=/dev/mmcblk0p${rootpartnum}" bootarg works by luck — across
reflashes the same physical card can come up as mmcblk0 OR mmcblk1, and
the kernel hangs in "Waiting for root device" when the race goes the
"wrong" way.

Setting "aliases { mmc0 = &sdhi0; mmc1 = &sdhi1; }" forces the mmc core
to honour the alias when allocating the mmcblk index (of_alias_get_id
in drivers/mmc/core/host.c), making numbering deterministic regardless
of probe-completion order:
  mmcblk0 ↔ sdhi0 ↔ 0x11c00000 (boot SDHI per the SMARC SoM design)
  mmcblk1 ↔ sdhi1 ↔ 0x11c10000

U-Boot's "mmc 0" view, the slot-udev rules (KERNEL=="mmcblk0pN"), the
RAUC system.conf slot devices, and the rauc_set_bootargs macro all line
up with the same enumeration after this patch — they had been
implicitly assuming this alignment.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-policy: SoM-specific mmc routing]
Signed-off-by: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/rzg2l-smarc-som.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/rzg2l-smarc-som.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/rzg2l-smarc-som.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/rzg2l-smarc-som.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/rzg2l-smarc-som.dtsi
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@
 / {
 	aliases {
 		ethernet0 = &eth0;
 		ethernet1 = &eth1;
+		mmc0 = &sdhi0;
+		mmc1 = &sdhi1;
 	};

 	chosen {
